laurel 2979: the panel commands go through the FIFO when the command buffer is above 4 GiB

[V] The cause of `LAUREL BACKLIGHT: off: DSI command DMA does not complete`, on some boots only: the buffer comes from above 4 GiB (log: buf 0x1b4664000) in spite of the mask, and DSI register 0x048 holds 32 bits. Boots that pass already end on the FIFO path (line `DCS HS, DMA at line 1568, FIFO`). [U] why the mask does not hold in IOBufferMemoryDescriptor on this kernel; the other users of this mask are bigger buffers with their own checks.

